 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\n\ne Streetlights (for example, address, property status, operation types)\n\nThe energy price is calculated in connection with the burning hour calendar.\n\ne Heating installations (for example, device category description, charging control, special agreements)\n\ne Container\n\nIntegration\n\nIntegrated Components and Their Functions\n\nThe following components are integrated to control reading and billing:\n\nComponent\n\nRegional Structure (ISU-BFRS)\n\nPortioning and Scheduling (ISU-BFPS)\n\nRate Structure (ISU-BIBDRS)\n\nInstallation Structure (ISU-DMDIIS)\n\nProfiles\n\nFunction\n\nFor streets or cities, you can define the temperature area and meter\n\nreading unit in the regional structure, and copy these default values\nto the installation.\n\nThe scheduling defines the meter reading dates. They depend on\nthe meter reading unit to which the installation is assigned.\n\nThe rate according to which the installation is billed depends on the\n\ngeneral rate category to which the installation is assigned. You can\nuse the individual rate category of the installation to override the\n\ngeneral rate category (for example, if you have made customer-\nspecific agreements).\n\nThe registers and rate data of devices that are installed in the\ninstallation are maintained in the installation structure.\n\nYou can assign load profiles to an installation. The assignment refers to the identification of the corresponding load profile.\n\nRegional Structure Default\n\nYou can use the regional structure defaults to have the system suggest the franchise contract. For this, you select the time slice to\n\nbe processed and choose |Edit } Region Defaults\n\nDeregulation Data\n\nThe entries that you make in the Deregulation Fields of the installation affect the determination of the Deregulation Scenario.\n\nOther\n\nYou can change the date Valid From or the premise of a utility installation provided that the utility installation has not yet been\nassigned a contract and no devices have been installed in the utility installation.\n\nPoint of Delivery (PoD)\n",
